Looking at the artifact, the core defect is that `flow()` never clears the `cart` (and related) session attributes between iterations. The `login()` chain clears many attributes but **not** `cart`, `etag`, `reservation`, `jobState`, `patchStatus`, `catalogStatus`, `expiryStatus`, `renewStatus`, `workStatus`, `retryAfter`, `recoveryCart`, `recoveryEtag`, `formCsrf`, `location`, `challengeHtml`, `challengeAction`, `challengeToken`, `nextPage`, `catalogBody`, `pollUrl`, `product`, `variant`, `grant`.

Because `cart` survives, the `doIf(!session.contains("cart"))` guard skips cart creation on iteration 2, so the second iteration reuses the completed cart → duplicate order / stale cart. Also `etag`, `reservation`, `jobState` leak across iterations.

Fix: make `login()` (which runs at the start of every journey) clear all per-journey state, including `cart`, `etag`, `reservation`, `jobState`, `patchStatus`, `catalogStatus`, `expiryStatus`, `renewStatus`, `workStatus`, `retryAfter`, `recoveryCart`, `recoveryEtag`, `catalogBody`, `pollUrl`, `formCsrf`, `location`, `challengeHtml`, `challengeAction`, `challengeToken`, `nextPage`, `product`, `variant`, `grant`. Also remove the `doIf(!session.contains("cart"))` guard so a fresh cart is always created per journey (the contract says "Every journey starts a fresh login/cart").

