Looking at the artifact, the core defect is in `row(Session)`: it always returns `rows.get(0)` (bench-1) regardless of the virtual user. With `exclusive_accounts: true` and 2 users, both users log in as bench-1, so the second login revokes the first user's session — exactly the "users invalidate each other's exclusive sessions" bug. The fix is to partition accounts by user id (and iteration), reading the fixture once and indexing per user.

I'll also make the fixture indexing robust (load once, index by `userId-1` modulo size, fall back to `bench-N`), and keep everything else intact.

