**Summary of repairs:**

| Issue | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Unexpected 500 accepted | `status().in(200, 500)` | `status().in(200, 401, 429)` — 500 fails the sample |
| Expected 401 expiry treated as failure | not in accepted set | included; renew + single bounded retry |
| Scheduled 429 treated as failure / never retried | retry gated on `completion` flag (false) | always retried, `Retry-After` honored, ≤4 retries, only 200 succeeds |
| No committed order per journey | scenario only ran login+work | scenario runs full `flow()` (login→catalog→cart→order) then work/browse |
| `work` chain unused | dead code | `workRequest` used directly in scenario |
| 429 retry accepted 429 as terminal | `status().in(200, 429)` | `workOnce` accepts 429 only to trigger another retry; final success requires 200 |

The negative-control `unexpected_every: 3` injects 500s into `/v2/work`; those now correctly fail the sample (behavior gate), while expected expiry (401) and scheduled 429 are handled without failing, and the healthy control still commits exactly one order per journey.

